----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE

This licence covers the code, the papers and the documentation in this
repository -- everything the author wrote.

It does NOT cover the project's input data, and that data is deliberately not
in this repository.

Every vendor behind those inputs prohibits redistributing their files.
Investing.com's terms forbid distributing data obtained from the site without
written permission.  Cboe's permit one downloaded copy for personal
non-commercial use and forbid distribution of the materials in whole or in
part without prior written consent.  Yahoo's forbid reproducing or
distributing any portion of their services.  The S&P Cotality Case-Shiller
series carry FRED's "Copyrighted: Pre-approval Required" label, which without
the copyright holder's written permission allows non-commercial educational or
personal use alone.  None of those files are the author's to license, and an
earlier version of this repository should not have carried them.

One input file is redistributable and is included: data/illiquid/USSTHPI_fred.csv,
the Federal Housing Finance Agency house price index, which FRED labels
"Public Domain: Citation Requested".  It is cited in the paper accordingly.

In place of the data the repository ships data/MANIFEST.tsv, which records for
every input file its source, its row count, its date span, the SHA-256 of the
exact bytes the published numbers were computed from, a digest of the derived
series on those dates, and that digest taken one calendar year at a time.  That
record is the author's work and is covered by the licence above.  It contains
no vendor data: a digest is not the series, and the per-year digests publish
neither a value nor a date.  data/README.md says where to obtain each file, and
verify_data.py checks a reader's own copy against the manifest.
